        "content": "Make a video explaining how password reset works in our web app: the user says they forgot their password, the app looks up their account, emails them a one-time link, and the user opens it and chooses a new password."
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "I've drafted the graph and saved it. It has five parts: the user, the web app, the user database and the email service, which sits outside your app. The flow runs from the user's request, to the account lookup, to the emailed link, to the new password being saved.\n\nI assumed the user database is part of your app's backend, and that the new password is saved to that database.\n\nIs this graph right? If so, I'll agree the story with you next. If not, tell me what to change.",
        "toolCalls": []
      },
