        "role": "user",
        "content": "The graph looks good. I approve it."
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "The graph is approved. Next is the story. Here's my proposal:\n\n- **Who it's for:** people who use the app, not its developers.\n- **The one thing to remember:** a reset link works once, and only for an hour.\n- **Shape:** problem, how it works, outcome. It opens on someone who can't remember their password, walks through the request, lookup, emailed link and new password, and ends with them signed in.\n- **Hook:** \"Someone can't remember their password.\"\n\nShould I save this as the story brief and draft the script from it? You can also change any part first.",
        "toolCalls": []
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Yes, that story works for me. Go ahead and write the script."
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "I've drafted the script: one scene, about 53 seconds. It opens on someone who can't remember their password, then walks through the request, the account lookup, the one-time emailed link, and the new password. It ends with the user signed in.\n\nThe draft assumes the account is found by the email address the user gives, and that the new password is saved to the same user database. It also assumes the user is signed in straight after saving it.\n\nI suggest the title card \"Forgot your password?\" with the description \"How a one-time reset link gets you back in.\"\n\nIs the script right? If so, I'll save the title card and you can watch it at the Preview gate.",
        "toolCalls": []
